# QA Playwright Standards

You are a **QA automation expert**. All automation code in this project must be **TypeScript** only (`.ts`). Never introduce `.js` test or page-object files.

## Locators

- **Always** use Playwright-provided locators (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByText`, `getByPlaceholder`, `getByAltText`, `getByTitle`, `getByTestId`, and locator chaining/filtering).
- **Never** use absolute XPath (e.g. `/html/body/div[1]/...`) or brittle `page.locator('xpath=...')` built from full paths.
- Prefer role + accessible name over CSS. Use `getByTestId` only when no accessible locator exists.
- Relative XPath is also discouraged; rewrite with Playwright locators instead.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — absolute XPath / raw CSS-heavy selectors
await page.locator('xpath=/html/body/div[1]/button[2]').click();
await page.locator('#root > div.container > button.submit').click();

// ✅ GOOD — Playwright locators
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();
await page.getByLabel('Email').fill('user@example.com');
```

## Page Object Model (POM)

- Enforce the **Page Object Model**: specs orchestrate flows; page objects own locators and actions.
- Put page objects under `pages/` (e.g. `pages/HomePage.ts`). Specs live under `tests/`.
- Page classes accept `Page` in the constructor, expose intent-based methods, and **do not** assert business outcomes (assertions stay in specs unless a dedicated assertion helper is shared).

```typescript
// pages/DocsPage.ts
import { type Page, type Locator } from '@playwright/test';

export class DocsPage {
  readonly getStarted: Locator;

  constructor(private readonly page: Page) {
    this.getStarted = page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Get started' });
  }

  async open(): Promise<void> {
    await this.page.goto('https://playwright.dev/');
  }

  async goToGetStarted(): Promise<void> {
    await this.getStarted.click();
  }
}

// tests/docs.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
import { DocsPage } from '../pages/DocsPage';

test('get started', async ({ page }) => {
  const docs = new DocsPage(page);
  await docs.open();
  await docs.goToGetStarted();
  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Installation' })).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Checklist before finishing a change

- [ ] TypeScript only
- [ ] No absolute XPath (or xpath-based locators)
- [ ] Playwright-provided locators only
- [ ] New UI interactions go through a page object, not inline in the spec
